# python-pyparsing -- flatpak's variant-schema compiler is written against it,
# and meson stops at configure without it:
#
#     flatpak-1.16.1/meson.build:266:2: ERROR: Problem encountered:
#     python3 "pyparsing" module is required
#
# NOT A TEST DEPENDENCY. flatpak is configured -Dtests=false here, and this is
# still required: the schema compiler generates C source that the build then
# compiles, so it runs on every build regardless of what is enabled.
#
# The fifth package existing only because Duct's python is built
# --without-ensurepip, after setuptools, mako, pyyaml and pycparser. Every one
# was found by a build stopping.
#
# EXCEPT THIS ONE WAS NOT. tools/check-recipes.sh has warned about it since
# flatpak was written, by name, with the reason attached:
#
#     flatpak: build may need the Python module 'pyparsing', which no recipe
#     provides (expected python-pyparsing).
#
# It is a WARNING rather than a problem, so it does not fail select, and it was
# read past every time -- including by me, quoting "0 problems" from a run whose
# warnings I had filtered out of my own report. A WARNING THAT PREDICTS A BUILD
# FAILURE IS A PROBLEM WEARING A LOWER SEVERITY. The check was right, the
# severity was arguably not, and the consumer was wrong.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/source/p/pyparsing/pyparsing-3.3.2.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=c777f4d763f140633dcb6d8a3eda953bf7a214dc4eff598413c070bcdc117cbc
SRC_DIR=pyparsing-3.3.2

PKG_ARCH=any
